>
>     I think there was some hacking around with RSX on the Pro series,
>     but never a version that really supported some of the Pro peculiar
>     hardware, like the video card.

Actually, P/OS and RSX use the same source files, where it makes sense. 
The P/OS stuff is conditional code in there.
However, some code is P/OS specific, such as device drivers, and some 
kernel modules. And those are (obviously) not shipped with standard RSX, 
so no way to build a P/OS system from RSX.
There was also a some kind of bridge system for P/OS development. 
Possibly mostly used before the hardware existed, but I'm not sure. You 
can find comments about it in the RSX sources.

>     I didn't know there was an RT-11 that ran on Pro, I wonder where I
>     could find it and whether it would run in that 350?  I don't
>     recall seeing it at Trailing Edge, but I wasn't looking for it,
>     either.

Yes. It exist, and was actually more or less officially released by DEC. 
It's not really a separate product or so, but just plain RT-11, with 
device drivers for the PRO specific hardware. I think it might even be 
in the official normal RT-11 distribution. But someone who knows RT-11 
better than me should comment on this.

And if Megan Gentry ever sees this, she can definitely comment on it.

