YES!!  RT-11 runs on the all of the PRO325, PRO350 and PRO380.
It is the official DEC distributed version of RT-11 which runs on all
Qbus and Unibus hardware as well - EXCEPT that the disk device
drivers are specifically for the CTI bus and there are ONLY two,
namely DW (for the hard disk drive - RD51 and RD52) and DZ
for the RX50 (assuming that I don't have the names switched).

IN  ADDITION,  as Johnny has mentioned, there is a PRO specific
device driver, PI(X).SYS, which is required to handle the video card
and clock interrupts, to mention just two of the hardware differences.
There may be others, but I have never looked very hard at the code
in PI(X).SYS since the PRO has never been my favourite hardware.

On the other hand, I will eventually look very closely at the code.
If anyone has a specific question, let me know.

>> And if Megan Gentry ever sees this, she can definitely comment on it.
>
I doubt that Megan will see this post.  I believe that she no longer
monitors RT-11.  However, Megan if you see this, please confirm.

> Forgot to say - yes, it should work fine on both the 325, 350 and 380.

Correct.

> As Bill Pechter mentioned in another reply, you just had to boot the 
> right disk, and set things up.
> Not sure if 5.7 was distributed in a way that could be booted on a 
> PRO, but I believe getting it running on the PRO should still be possible.

The most frequent standard DEC RT-11 distribution for a hard drive was
for the RL02.  With 20,450 blocks, RT-11 was able to fit quite comfortably
on that media.  The other media was usually 9-track tape.  Since the PRO
is unable to support either of these media, making up RX50 floppy diskettes
is probably the only way to initially boot RT-11 on a PRO.  That turns out
to be relatively simple since DEC provided a standard command file to
facilitate that procedure, at least that is what I seem to remember.  What
I can't remember is if there was a PRO specific variation.  However, anyone
who can produce an RX50 boot diskette for the Qbus can also produce
a second variation of the same diskette for the PRO using the standard
RT-11 commands.

For who is interested:
COPY/DEVICE/NOQU   DU0:  DU1:
COPY/BOOT:DZ  DU1:RT11FB.SYS  DU1:

If the diskette on DU0: is able to boot and an RX50 on a Qbus system,
the diskette on DU1: should be able to boot on a PRO system with an
RX50 - assuming that I remember my RT-11 commands correctly.

Please let us know if it works - or does not work and we can try again.

Jerome Fine


