> Forgot to mention: The other problem with a lot of available chips if
> you're interfacing to anything modern is that many modern devices
> (especially FPGAs) can't take more than 3.3v on their inputs.

   Well, one could always put a set of level translators in there.  Two 
MOSFETs would do the trick, but there are nice wide 74xx series chips 
