As VAXman has already noted, VGA to 5BNC cables are available
commercially and do the same job; I bought one recently at a very
reasonable price when I bent a pin beyond repair on the one I'd been
using.

HOWEVER: is there an unstated implication behind the stated question?
Old monitors with 3*BNC are going to want sync on green. Modern
graphics cards don't (afaik) generally do sync on green. How's your
electronics?

Wrt LCD monitors which will work with Alphas: you may need to say what
kind of Alpha, and specifically what kind of graphics card (and your
preferred graphics mode), before people can give you informed answers.


