I'm not 110% sure but afaik, besides the ZLXp-E*/PBXGA-* there are
very few PCI cards that can do sync on green AND with VMS support.

This card family also has switches for resolution and refresh rate, a
facility which is occasionally useful but is as rare as rocking horse
output on more modern cards.

When these cards are in boxes with SRM console, there is a console
variable to enable/disable sync on green. Can't remember the name
right now but it's obvious once you see it (TGA_SYNC_ON_GREEN, maybe?).


