Since I have not had an occasion to use the PRO hardware in many
years, there has not been a reason to test V05.07 of RT-11 to determine
if it can boot on the PRO hardware.  On the other hand, all of the files,
PI(X).SYS, DW(X).SYS and DZ(X).SYS, required to execute "normal"
RT-11 on a PRO are present in the DEC distribution V05.07 for RT-11
in the same manner as other previous distributions of RT-11 which have
been booted on a PRO.

HOWEVER, as I already suggested, in order to boot an RX50 floppy
diskette on a PRO, there needs to be a VERY special command option
used to produce that floppy diskette when it is being produced on
NON-PRO hardware.  If anyone is interested, please ask how this
is done with an RX50 on a Qbus system running RT-11.  Alternatively,
Ersatz-11 can also produce the required RX50 floppy diskette on a
PC which has a 1.2 MB 5 1/4" HD floppy drive as long as DSDD
media is used - since normal HD 1.2 MB floppy media is for use in
an RX33 floppy drive.

Jerome Fine


