More specifically, you need to know the order of the blocks.

Among others, it seems that some double-side formats go from 
cylinder 0 to 76 on the first side, then from 76 back to 0 on
the second side.  That makes it easier to be compatible with
single side.  Maybe even 0 to 76 and then 0 to 76.

I thought the OP was able to read the disk with ordinary files,
though, but only had problems with the BACKUP disks.  That should
mean that the blocks are in the right order.

-- glen


