Well, even more, the software that defines the block order.

Do RX01 and RX02 do interleave?  In the 5.25in formats, it is usual
to interleave by writing the blocks with the appropriate sector
number in them.  In the 8in formats, where disks usually came
already formatted, it was more usual to keep the sector numbers,
but read them in a different order.  (At least CP/M does that.)

If the data is ASCII, then it might be possible to see from the
data which blocks should follow which other blocks.

-- glen


