E11 and my emulator both support a variable size disk device HD: which
reflects the size of the disk image mounted. E11 is probably the more
flexible option.

E11: http://www.dbit.com/
RUST: http://rust.wikispaces.com/

Of course, there may be other wrinkles.

Apart from that it might be possible to do some simple media
conversion which might be as simple as truncating the media files at
the required size depending on the psuedo media layout. Later versions
of RT-11 provide the utility SPLIT to simplify that operation. Of
course, it might be a bit more complicated than that (and usually is)
:-)




