On Mar 9, 1:42=A0pm, h...@unicorn.tsht.lan (Holm Tiffe) wrote:
> Hi,
> I have a QBUS Serpentine Backplane H9275-A here, there are 2 Connectors,
> J2 wich is a 10 Pin header and J3 which consists of 6 Screws.
>
> Does someone know the pinout for those connectors?
>
> On the other side is the power connector, it has labels for the pinning.
> I've searched the net for the EK-H927A-CG documentnt but haven't found
> it anywhere ...
>
> THX in andvance,
>
> Holm

check the documentation for H9270 and H 9273 backplanes. I believe
they are identical.
J3 is a power connector, starting from one side: +12v, +5v (usually a
red wire), +5v (usually bus bar jumpered to the adjacent +5), Gnd
(usually a black wire), Gnd, Blank.  The wires are usually TWNN
stranded 14 or 12 AWG.

The 10 pin connector carries the logical signals from the backplane to
the front panel and are as follows:
1- BPOK H
2- BEVNET L
3- SRUN L
4- Key
5- Gnd
6- CL3 L
7- CS3 L
8- Spare
9- BHALT L
10- DCOK H

You can double check these pin outs by checking continunity from the
connector pins to the corresponding backplane pins.

John


