> Not sure I follow you concern about the slew rate. 

I remember stories a long time ago, about DEC specifying a
maximum slew rate for the drivers.  Both reflections on the
bus and coupling between bus lines are problems at higher
rates.

> Are you saying the
> '760 has a higher slew rate than the original DEC drivers?  If so, I
> don't see that as a problem - its signals would be significantly less
> that the minimum setup times.  Ringing might be a concern, but if the
> bus is properly terminated then the potential problem would be
> mitigated.  If not, putting a small capacitor (10pf) on the output
> would slow the rise time.

A small series resistor can also be used.  Small enough that the
drop at maximum drive current isn't too big.  Though that works
better driving MOS inputs, it should still be possible.

-- glen
 


