David Riley <fraveydank@gmail.com> wrote:
> On Mar 15, 7:19�pm, legalize+jee...@mail.xmission.com (Richard) wrote:
>> What about using a "Field Programmable Analog Array" like the parts
>> described here?
>> <http://www.diodes.com/products/semicustom/700_series.html>
 
> Looks interesting, though that's not exactly field programmable; you
> can basically design the metal mask layer and have someone fab it.

(snip)

How about just using series termination?  A small resistor between
the output and the bus.  That slows down the transition, and also
helps absorb any reflections.

There are probably many web pages describing bus termination, but

http://www.fairchildsemi.com/an/AN/AN-393.pdf

is the first one I found on a search.

This one describes both TTL and 74HC.  

The 74HCT devices would be interesting possibilities for
replacements for Qbus drivers.  

-- glen


