(snip, someone wrote)
>>> This sounds interesting.
>>> However, If I remember correct, there was a thread recently discussing
>>> missing driver chips for Q-BUS, they seem no longer be available.

>> (snip)

(then I wrote)
>> The 74LVC2245A sounds interesting.
 
> I was mistaken, the correct levels are Vil of 1.3V, and Vih of 1.7V

Usual for TTL is 0.8V and 2.0V.  That is what most specify.

The DS8641 specifies receiver threshold for the bus side
as Vih min 1.70V typ 1.50V and Vil as typ 1.50V max 1.30V.

Since it is usual for the minimum to be lass, and the maximum
to be more than the typical, that seems strange.  But then
they have other mistakes, like getting current and voltage
mixed up.  Vol is 16ma, for example.

-- glen


