Nope. Sadly they are just the same. The problem is that the interrupt 
hardware design and the bus works rather different on the PRO than on 
any other PDP-11. And of course, you have the bitmapped graphics that is 
your normal console...

It is also very annoying that you cannot run any more fullblown version 
on the 380, as the CPU have more capabilities, but POS just don't let 
you use them. So, no supervisor mode libraries, and no split I/D-space. :-(

